  "notes": [
   "The catalog lists courses under discipline headings (Addiction Studies, Administrative Justice, Agriculture, Anthropology, Business, Communication Studies, Early Childhood Education, Economics, Education, Ethnic Studies, Geography, Health Education, Health Science, History, Nursing, Philosophy, Physical Education Theory, Political Science, Psychology, Social Justice Studies, Sociology, Theatre & Cinema), each 'Complete ANY of the following Courses'. Recorded as one choose_units block of 18 units, per the rule 'For the 18 units required, select courses from at least two disciplines; from one of the disciplines select at least two courses.' The discipline-distribution rule is not captured by the block structure.",
   "total_units 18 is taken from the sentence 'For the 18 units required'; the page prints no separate major-total line. Reviewer should confirm.",
   "degree_total 60 from 'Total Required Credits 60'. GE pattern is Local GE; no GE units printed.",
   "Electives (Courses Numbered 1-199) are required when degree units plus GE units total fewer than 60; no elective units printed, so electives_fill_degree is true.",
   "The catalog prints no units beside any course; all units are null (the state file lists 3 units for most, 4 for PSY 9).",
   "Codes are recorded as printed without spaces (e.g., AOD1 for closed-list AOD 1, POLSC1000 for POLS C1000, PSYCC1000 for PSYC C1000) and matched to the closed list.",
   "Closed list has both 'NRN 70' and 'NRN70'; both correspond to the single printed NRN70, which has NVN70 as its 'OR' alternative.",
   "GEG1, PSY42, SJS21 and TAC7 are printed as bare codes without titles; recorded as catalog additions along with HES2, HISTC1002, HIS55 and PHL5.",
   "Students can double count General Education courses with the area of emphasis.",
   "No program learning outcomes or careers are printed in this text."
